                <pb facs="0315" n="213" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg213"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.3421/41: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-07-23T13:00:00-03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 23, 1918, 1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 24, 3.59
                            a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Confidential. Department’s June 24, 2 p.m. Forwarded today in pouch number 20 by
                    cruiser <hi rendition="#italic">Montevideo</hi> text of Vickers Armstrong
                    proposition, which would close the open door, covering 55-year monopoly of
                    construction steel plant, shipyards, et cetera, with important ramifications.
                    Itabira not controlling factor in awarding contract.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
